  "term": "Satanism",
  "definition": "In this source, Satanism refers to a locally held supernatural explanation for childhood anaemia. It is described as a personalistic cause of illness, distinct from natural causes such as malaria or poor nutrition, and believed to be addressed through prayer rather than hospital care.",
